      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖a‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖a‖ & =\\sqrt{{a}_{1}^{2}+{a}_{2}^{2}+{a}_{3}^{2}+{a}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
