      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given $x=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖x‖.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
