    "q-39761": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39761",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Find the distance between the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $0.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,0) & =‖x-0‖ \\\\  & =‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(20)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+400+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{441} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
