    "q-74120": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74120",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given the vectors $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$, find the distance $\\text{d}(u,v).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the distance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(u,v) & =‖u-v‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({u}_{1}-{v}_{1})^{2}+({u}_{2}-{v}_{2})^{2}+({u}_{3}-{v}_{3})^{2}+({u}_{4}-{v}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-3)^{2}+(-1-(-1))^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(2-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
